    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0033" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710. Consultation 4/4–646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Adam</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">u.s. urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-06T19:00:00-04:00">April 6, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. Foreign Minister<anchor n="38" xml:id="d17-f1"/> personally handed me 1-page
                    memo on Argentine consultation at 7 p.m. Résumé as follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Reiterated its memo of Dec. 27, 1945 to this Embassy re erroneous or
                            incomplete information on political situation of American countries
                            which cause judgments [not in?] accordance reality.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>As it is principal interest strengthen American solidarity based on
                            agreements atmosphere of misconfidence must vanish.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>San Francisco Security Pact in order to have regional manifestation in
                            mutual assistance treaty must not exclude any of its members so as to
                            guarantee its effectiveness.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Bolivian Govt feels new conditions for finding complete continental
                            solidarity have arisen as result Argentine elections.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Bolivian Govt declares it will continue to maintain same cordial
                            relations with Argentine Govt as has marked its policy towards all
                            nations of the Continent.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="38" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p>The Acting Foreign Minister, Col. José Celestino Pinto.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
